{"name":"Messenger Bag","hex":"#7d745e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"messenger bag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sack worn over one shoulder with a strap winding around the chest, traditionally used by bicycle messengers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/messenger_bag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Messenger bag","blocks":[{"text":"A messenger bag is a type of sack, usually made of cloth. It is worn over one shoulder with a strap that goes across the chest resting the bag on the lower back. While messenger bags are sometimes used by couriers, they are now also an urban fashion icon. Some types of messenger bags are called carryalls. A smaller version is often called a sling bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Timbuk2_custom-made_messenger_bag_%E2%80%9EDeeDog%E2%80%9C.JPG/330px-Timbuk2_custom-made_messenger_bag_%E2%80%9EDeeDog%E2%80%9C.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Messenger_bag","wikidata":"Q890094"},{"title":"Bag","blocks":[{"text":"A bag, also known regionally as a sack or tote, is a common tool in the form of a floppy container, typically made of cloth, leather, bamboo, paper, or plastic. The use of bags predates recorded history, with the earliest bags being lengths of animal skin, cotton, or woven plant fibers, folded up at the edges and secured in that shape with strings of the same material. Bags can be used to carry items such as personal belongings, groceries, tools, and other objects. They come in various shapes and sizes, often equipped with handles or straps for easier carrying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg/330px-Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bag","wikidata":"Q1323314"}],"images":[{